1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,548
Up to now, you've been writing a universe with enemies in it,

2
00:00:03,998 --> 00:00:06,110
and letting the game decide how many.

3
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:08,333
Today you take that over.

4
00:00:10,133 --> 00:00:14,717
By the end, you'll know how many ships are waiting in every kind of system,

5
00:00:15,167 --> 00:00:17,504
and which line of which file put them there.

6
00:00:18,404 --> 00:00:19,628
And you'll have a budget,

7
00:00:20,078 --> 00:00:22,115
a number you wrote down on purpose.

8
00:00:23,315 --> 00:00:26,505
There are only three places an enemy ship comes from.

9
00:00:28,305 --> 00:00:30,358
One is an enemy system,

10
00:00:30,808 --> 00:00:33,799
the kind the game rolls from your mixes in Lecture Five.

11
00:00:34,699 --> 00:00:37,588
Two is a foe's home, where their station is.

12
00:00:38,488 --> 00:00:40,844
And three is a landmark with guards on it.

13
00:00:42,644 --> 00:00:44,556
You've already written all three.

14
00:00:45,456 --> 00:00:47,526
What you haven't done is count them.

15
00:00:48,726 --> 00:00:51,666
Enemies come in fleets, and a fleet has a tier,

16
00:00:52,116 --> 00:00:53,319
from one to eleven.

17
00:00:54,219 --> 00:00:58,002
This table is how many ships are in one fleet, at each tier,

18
00:00:58,452 --> 00:01:00,726
for each of the six kinds of ship.

19
00:01:02,526 --> 00:01:03,584
Follow the Torgoth row.

20
00:01:04,484 --> 00:01:07,020
It's one ship at the bottom, three in the middle,

21
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:09,068
and six at the top.

22
00:01:09,968 --> 00:01:12,803
And the ships get heavier as the fleet gets bigger.

23
00:01:13,703 --> 00:01:14,704
At the top tier,

24
00:01:15,154 --> 00:01:17,451
that's six of the largest thing they fly.

25
00:01:18,651 --> 00:01:20,151
So what sets the tier?

26
00:01:21,051 --> 00:01:23,752
One number, called Difficulty,

27
00:01:24,202 --> 00:01:27,900
and it lives in the settings file, where you named your ship back in Class One.

28
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,925
Here's what it does to one enemy system.

29
00:01:32,825 --> 00:01:34,830
At five, there are six ships.

30
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,818
At eight there are eleven,

31
00:01:37,268 --> 00:01:40,038
and at eleven there are twenty-four.

32
00:01:41,838 --> 00:01:45,179
It grows that fast because Difficulty counts twice.

33
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:47,934
It sets how many fleets there are,

34
00:01:48,384 --> 00:01:50,683
and it sets the tier of every one of them.

35
00:01:52,483 --> 00:01:55,737
My universe is a backwater with one ship in it,

36
00:01:56,187 --> 00:01:57,529
so I'm setting it to four.

37
00:01:58,729 --> 00:02:01,383
In Lecture Five you put guards on the Bone Pile,

38
00:02:01,833 --> 00:02:03,381
with just the kind of ship.

39
00:02:04,281 --> 00:02:07,067
Written like that, the guards follow Difficulty.

40
00:02:08,867 --> 00:02:13,671
Put a number after the word, and that's their tier, whatever Difficulty says.

41
00:02:14,571 --> 00:02:18,373
Seven is three Torgoth ships, every time.

42
00:02:20,173 --> 00:02:22,260
And I'm adding a small guard to the Tern,

43
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:25,341
because somebody is picking at that wreck.

44
00:02:27,141 --> 00:02:29,329
There are four things to know about guards.

45
00:02:30,229 --> 00:02:32,264
The crew gets a warning, on Comms.

46
00:02:33,164 --> 00:02:36,188
The guards wait by the landmark, not by the crew.

47
00:02:37,088 --> 00:02:40,090
They're raiders, so no ceasefire calls them off.

48
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:43,086
And once they're destroyed, they stay gone.

49
00:02:44,286 --> 00:02:47,729
A foe's home always has one fleet, at the Difficulty,

50
00:02:48,179 --> 00:02:49,602
and it waits close.

51
00:02:50,502 --> 00:02:54,296
It's the one place your crew arrives with the enemy already on top of them.

52
00:02:56,096 --> 00:02:58,758
There's also something there you didn't write.

53
00:02:59,658 --> 00:03:01,180
Most of the times I visited,

54
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:04,629
the station launched four fighters of its own.

55
00:03:05,529 --> 00:03:07,380
No line of yours sets that number,

56
00:03:07,830 --> 00:03:09,976
so just add four when you count.

57
00:03:11,176 --> 00:03:14,638
There are two more dials, and they go in the story file,

58
00:03:15,088 --> 00:03:18,140
right under the two travel lines from Lecture Two.

59
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:21,176
It's a card, so copy it from the page.

60
00:03:21,626 --> 00:03:25,093
The only words you change are the two in quote marks.

61
00:03:26,893 --> 00:03:28,568
The first is Danger.

62
00:03:29,468 --> 00:03:31,432
It doesn't add ships to a system.

63
00:03:31,882 --> 00:03:34,447
It makes more systems enemy systems.

64
00:03:35,347 --> 00:03:37,138
From quiet to dangerous,

65
00:03:37,588 --> 00:03:41,002
mine went from fourteen enemy systems to fifty-four.

66
00:03:42,802 --> 00:03:45,291
The second is Encounters.

67
00:03:46,191 --> 00:03:49,229
Dormant puts an enemy system's fleets at the far edge,

68
00:03:49,679 --> 00:03:53,891
so the crew gets time to talk before the shooting starts.

69
00:03:55,691 --> 00:03:58,964
Spell both words exactly as they are on the page.

70
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:01,664
A wrong word isn't an error.

71
00:04:02,114 --> 00:04:04,920
It's just the gentle setting, and nobody tells you.

72
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,447
Now add it up, for your worst system.

73
00:04:09,347 --> 00:04:10,976
Mine is the Bone Pile.

74
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:15,111
At Difficulty four it holds four Gleaner ships,

75
00:04:15,561 --> 00:04:17,627
and three guards, so that's seven.

76
00:04:18,527 --> 00:04:20,787
At eleven it would be twenty-seven.

77
00:04:22,587 --> 00:04:24,404
So how many is too many?

78
00:04:25,304 --> 00:04:26,550
Here's what's known so far.

79
00:04:27,450 --> 00:04:30,443
A system only exists while a crew is in it.

80
00:04:31,343 --> 00:04:33,624
So what counts is your worst system,

81
00:04:34,074 --> 00:04:37,971
times the crews that can be in different systems at once.

82
00:04:39,771 --> 00:04:42,866
The people who make the game pushed it until it slowed down,

83
00:04:43,316 --> 00:04:47,120
and that was at about a hundred and ninety ships fighting at once,

84
00:04:47,570 --> 00:04:49,096
with no consoles connected.

85
00:04:49,996 --> 00:04:52,694
Nobody has measured it with a full bridge.

86
00:04:53,594 --> 00:04:56,220
So stay a long way under that number.

87
00:04:57,420 --> 00:05:00,015
Lint says clean, for all six files.

88
00:05:00,915 --> 00:05:03,473
But lint doesn't read the settings file at all,

89
00:05:03,923 --> 00:05:06,387
so read the checklist on the page.

90
00:05:08,187 --> 00:05:09,184
Now let's fly it.

91
00:05:10,084 --> 00:05:11,755
First we go to the Tern,

92
00:05:12,205 --> 00:05:14,898
and there's her card, and the warning on Comms.

93
00:05:15,798 --> 00:05:17,772
And then the Gleaners' home.

94
00:05:18,672 --> 00:05:19,971
This is what close looks like.

95
00:05:21,171 --> 00:05:22,174
Now it's your turn.

96
00:05:23,074 --> 00:05:26,853
Decide who your game is for, and set Difficulty to match.

97
00:05:27,753 --> 00:05:29,887
List every system your story visits,

98
00:05:30,337 --> 00:05:32,955
and count the three sources for each one.

99
00:05:33,855 --> 00:05:36,496
Then write your budget at the top of your file.

100
00:05:38,296 --> 00:05:40,981
Next time, we stage a battle ourselves,

101
00:05:41,431 --> 00:05:44,666
at one place, at the moment the story gets there.
